# Jones International Bank SOC

Cloud-native security analytics and threat detection platform built on AWS EC2.

## Overview

Jones International Bank SOC is a senior cybersecurity capstone project designed to simulate an end-to-end Security Operations Center workflow.

The environment combines a Flask-based fintech application, structured application logging, Python ingestion workflows, real-world PISCES security telemetry, and OpenSearch dashboards for security monitoring and investigation.

## Architecture

Authenticated Users / Simulated Attackers
        ↓
Flask Fintech Application
        ↓
JSON Security Logs
        ↓
Python Ingestion Pipeline
        ↓
Detection & Analysis
        ↓
OpenSearch
        ↓
SOC Dashboards & Investigation

## Technologies

- AWS EC2
- Linux
- OpenSearch
- Python
- Flask
- Suricata
- JSON
- SQLite
- Docker

## Key Features

- Authentication and MFA
- Financial transaction simulation
- Administrative functionality
- Fraud review workflow
- Structured security-event logging
- Security telemetry ingestion
- Custom OpenSearch indexes
- Threat investigation dashboards
- Analysis of initial access, command-and-control, scanning, exploit activity, and authentication events

## What I Built

I configured the AWS-hosted environment, installed and configured OpenSearch, developed the Flask banking simulator, generated structured security events, imported real-world PISCES telemetry, built Python ingestion workflows, created custom OpenSearch indexes, and developed dashboards for investigation and security monitoring.

## Security Operations Workflow

The project follows an end-to-end analyst workflow:

1. Generate application and attack activity
2. Capture structured security logs
3. Ingest and normalize telemetry
4. Analyze events using OpenSearch
5. Identify suspicious patterns and attack categories
6. Investigate events using dashboards and detailed records
7. Prioritize findings for analyst review

## Project Goals

The goal was to understand how a modern SOC works beyond simply reviewing existing alerts by building the environment that generates, ingests, analyzes, and presents security telemetry.

## Disclaimer

This project was developed in a controlled academic and lab environment for cybersecurity education and authorized security analysis.
